criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Adult patients aged 18 to 60 years;
* Presenting a primary anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) tear;
* Scheduled for ACL reconstruction associated with MacIntosh-type lateral extra-articular tenodesis (or equivalent technical variant using an iliotibial band 'ITB' graft);
* Surgery to be performed under general anesthesia;
* Planned management in outpatient surgery or short-stay hospitalization after the operation;
* Understanding the validated French version of the QoR-15 questionnaire;
* Having given their informed consent to participate in the study;
* Patients affiliated with or benefiting from a social security scheme.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Patients having allergy to local anesthetics or a contraindication to peripheral nerve blocks;
* Patients having neuropathy of the lower limbs;
* Patients having coagulation disorders or on major anticoagulation;
* Patients suffering from chronic pain that requires more than 30 mg morphine-equivalents per day;
* Patients undergoing revision ACL reconstruction;
* Patients with pre-existing hypoesthesia of the lateral thigh (e.g. known meralgia paresthetica);
* Patients unable to complete the questionnaires or expressing refusal to participate;
* Pregnant women, women of childbearing age without effective contraception), or women breastfeeding;
* Protected adults under guardianship, curatorship or other legal protection, deprived of liberty or under guardianship or curatorship, or unable to give consent.
